## Context

Author question during the 0283 proofread (2026-07-29): should works without
a language tag be removed, as no-title works are? Probe of the frozen v2
refined corpus (33,344 works):

- **language blank: 9.** Six bibCNRS Chinese works with full metadata
  (titles, authors, years, DOIs) — langdetect skipped them (no abstract);
  remedy is tagging `zh`, not removal. Three OpenAlex oddities: a title-less
  record with author/year/DOI (W1558763458), an author-less chapter stub
  "J. Climate Finance" (W7132781315), a 2025 "Green Climate Fund" record.
- **first_author blank: 543 (1.6%).** Teaching canon 228, OpenAlex 249;
  samples are institutional/corporate documents where personal authorship
  does not exist. Gap is corporate authorship not carried, not junk.
- **year blank: 389 (1.2%).** Teaching 214, OpenAlex 132, SciSpace 46;
  SciSpace subset includes title-less rows worth per-record review.
- **Related, found in passing: 3,278 works dated outside 1990–2024**
  (2,752 in 2025, 485 in 2026, 1 in 2027, ~40 pre-1990 back to 1960) while
  title/abstract/§2.1 declare the window. Surfaced to the author separately;
  whatever the resubmission says, v3 needs a policy (enforce the window,
  or a documented exemption for lead-times and window-exempt layers).

## Actions

1. Author decides per facet: remove, repair (tag zh, carry corporate
   author, backfill year), or document as accepted missingness.
2. Implement in the filter/enrich pipeline with per-facet counts in the
   run report; refresh deposit descriptor missingness shares.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each blank-field facet has a decided, implemented, documented policy
- [ ] Year-window policy decided and enforced or documented
- [ ] v3 QA report shows the resulting counts